1
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:20,120
I have screwed a lot with drag racing when I was younger, kind of promod.

2
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:24,980
Also screwed up a bit with snowmobile drag racing.

3
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:27,640
I've always liked drag racing.

4
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:30,860
-What is you competing with?
Should we check what you have.

5
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:34,520
We can start with the veteran class.
Then you can have one here.

6
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:39,860
Sure you can have a finer but I have chosen it to look a little worn.

7
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,380
-Lite Rat Rod?
Yes.

8
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:46,660
Mechanically, it is in top condition.
All brakes and layers are replaced.

9
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:49,300
It is very nice condition even though it is not visible.

10
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:53,260
-70 numbers?
No all mopeds I have are 66or.

11
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:55,240
Sport Combinette 1966.

12
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:58,375
So it is -66 that applies?
Yes right now ...

13
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:00,640
I have a little newer too.

14
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:33,220
It is possible to stroke up to 72cc.

15
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:35,920
-What does it cost to trim?
Is it expensive?

16
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:41,360
Both yes and no.
It is a cheap sport to be motorsport.

17
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:45,000
Motorsport costs money but this is cheap.

18
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,900
I crashed a motor a week ago.

19
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,600
The block burst and the gearbox ...

20
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:55,360
It cost SEK 2500 to cook.
-Oh!

21
00:02:55,360 --> 00:03:00,200
A little drive and shoulders then you can drive again.

22
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:03,280
A car engine that breaks can cost SEK 75,000 to cook.

23
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,000
Absolutely!
Or more.

24
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,000
This one I bought far out in the woods a few miles from here.

25
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:52,260
-Do you run 200 meters?
Yes, 200 meters with a stationary start.

26
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,660
-How many gears do you have?
This one has four.

27
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:58,060
3-4 years ago, 3 drove.

28
00:04:58,060 --> 00:05:01,620
It was such a big step between 2an and 3an.

29
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,920
It is not suitable for drag racing.

30
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,320
Not if you are going to perform good times.

31
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:10,380
What I remembered from when I was young.
Now I didn't have Zundapp myself ...

32
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:16,260
... was that the gear slider had a long stroke.

33
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:19,200
Yes you hit the knee in the elbow.

34
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:23,020
That is why we who compete have gear stops.

35
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:24,560
-The gear stop?

36
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:38,620
I can't give all the mopeds love between the runs.

37
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:42,540
One or two is recommended.
-How very screw is it vs run?

38
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:45,060
Hmm ... change drives and nozzles ..

39
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:49,920
..The rusty I have been running so many years so I almost do not screw it.

40
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:53,160
Just pushed up a cog last time and it was probably the only thing.

41
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:58,380
This requires ignition adjustment, mouth cut ... ... there are so many adjustments left.

42
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:05,020
It can take 10 hours of driving before it goes 90% of its capacity.

43
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:10,400
The rusty is probably 100% of its capacity.
It is almost not possible to drive anything faster with it.

44
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:13,405
It is difficult.
But this is much left.

45
00:07:13,405 --> 00:07:16,540
This one should go faster than the rusty but it does not.

46
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:18,520
It's a long way to go yet.

47
00:09:21,780 --> 00:09:25,840
I have chosen to run a Zundapp engine on this with.

48
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:30,580
-What does a modern engine mean?
Yes you can have 6-gears.

49
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:34,080
Most of them are reed -fed original.

50
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:39,260
It is awesome and lightly trimmed engines.

51
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:42,740
This is a little more complicated.
-You hold you to Zundapp.

52
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:47,200
It would be to put on an AM6 engine on this.

53
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,360
Then I would rather get further down in the field.

54
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:52,880
This is a promod 50, ie 50cc.

55
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:56,760
The rusty is 66cc in the veteran 70 class.

56
00:09:56,760 --> 00:10:02,540
This one is quite exactly 70cc in the same class.

57
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:06,100
And this Promod 50 and it is about 50cc.

58
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:57,980
We are not dissected, they think it is cool so I hope more will start competing.

59
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:03,020
-What is the most fun to drive?
Right now it's the rusty one because it delivers.

60
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:06,025
After all, it is tested to the max.

61
00:13:06,025 --> 00:13:08,655
The other two I have a lot of work left.

62
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:10,840
-Both?
Yes both.

63
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:15,520
I tested it chassis last year and had this engine on.

64
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:20,480
Just to test the chassis and then I used this engine a polini that I ported myself.

65
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:25,300
I drove 10.3 and 105-106 km/h with that engine.

66
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:29,560
In this chassis and then I discovered that it had to be strengthened.

67
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:32,100
Trying to build as easily as possible but ...

68
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:36,400
... that engine twisted the entire chassis.

69
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:41,180
The chassis was too clumsy so I had to reinforce.

70
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:43,980
Last year you can say that chassis work well.

71
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:47,780
This year I have used the real engine but ...

72
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:49,815
... I have had problems with.

73
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:56,440
It sounds strange and I have scrapped some membrane and blown packing boxes when I drive nitrous oxide.

74
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:59,160
This is how there is ...

75
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:02,160
-How many people drive with nitrous oxide on mopeds?

76
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,800
Yes there are some pieces ...

77
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:08,380
... there are also those who drive with nitro in promod.

78
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:12,640
And those who drive with methanol.

79
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:15,000
It is quite unlimited in Promod.

80
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,280
-How is the buddy at the competitions?
It is very good.

81
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:22,280
-Ing hard rivalry?
No, it's a nice level.

82
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:27,400
There is no prestige.
Everyone knows everyone and we have fun in the evenings.

83
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:32,120
-You don't reveal your secrets?

84
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:37,980
A little bit so maybe, gate times etc ..

85
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:41,760
-When you trim do everything yourself?
I try to do everything myself.

86
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:46,840
I have built some pipes but have not got it really well.

87
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:50,620
Recently, I have bought ready -made that I have modified.

88
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:55,380
Contracted header, shortened and extended and made adjustments.

89
00:14:55,480 --> 00:15:03,100
So that it hangs like a snake in the ceiling.
Yes a little different pipes that I have tried over the years.

90
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:05,720
-How long holds a piston & cylinder?

91
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:09,560
That .. you talk about the rusty, huh?

92
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:15,640
I have been running it for 2 years and I changed piston ring this spring that's all.

93
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:20,520
Although it turns so much so it holds well.

94
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:23,000
-What is this?
It looks like...

95
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,100
Here I usually sit and port cylinders.

96
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:28,420
Isn't this a goldsmith usually use?

97
00:15:28,420 --> 00:15:30,500
Well, it's from an old workshop.

98
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,680
It is a little small sometimes and I have not been able to port coil.

99
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:41,320
Now I have found this and I think it is from the 60s.
It is old dental equipment.

100
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:47,280
Now I come down in the cylinders so I can change the coil.

101
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:51,960
-Where can you find such old stuff?
Think it was at Tradera.

102
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:55,100
You had one more moped over here is it also a Zundapp?

103
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:59,580
Yes it is a ride moped completely original.
Okay a utility lashes.

104
00:17:12,320 --> 00:17:13,920
-Is there any moped we can start?

105
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:18,100
Can start any.
We can start up the rusty.

106
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:23,400
Don't think people understand that there is a lot to drive when it looks like it does.

107
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:27,080
Absolutely, pick it up.

108
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:31,040
-Do you nice on that one?
No!

109
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:35,640
I usually train a lot of starts and get abrasions the inside of the thighs.

110
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:38,620
So it is not nice but all for the look.

111
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:34,740
14400 rpm.
Well I have alternated more sometimes.

112
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:39,060
Now it's cold so I don't want to torment it.

113
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:07,480
Damn!

114
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:08,780
Which moped.

115
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:40,600
There are some in Ö-vik, Lycksele and Bjäst.

116
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:43,120
Great name!
Easy.

117
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:57,120
Hahaha!
It sounds like a cross.

118
00:20:22,980 --> 00:20:27,780
16320 rpm, it's totally crazy.

119
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:29,720
-This is like a cross.

120
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:32,920
Yes the light is deceiving.

121
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,940
Hahaha, really!

122
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:38,620
It's totally crazy.
I didn't get the camera when you drove past.

123
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:45,060
A little missed gears when it is not a sharp position and you have foppa slippers.

124
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:47,200
Normally, the gears sit as they should.

125
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:51,000
Not many people do not think it should go fast when you see it.
It usually is so.

126
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:56,400
It has a lovely sound.
Yes it is straight in the clutch basket.

127
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,720
So it wines a little neighbor.

128
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,360
What a machine!

129
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:03,020
-How should you go if you want to start competing?

130
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:07,800
There are 2 pages on the Internet and Facebook.

131
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:12,180
Facebook: Swedish Moped Dragracing and Lyckseletwostroke.se

132
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:17,580
There you can read and ask questions.

133
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:19,500
Check out past events.

134
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:25,600
Then I think you should start competing.
There are so many sharp mopeds ...
